# r is a real variable and the post-expectation is r itself, negative at states the program
# never reaches.  A fair choice between r = 1.5 and r = 0.5 gives
#   wp(S, r) = 1/2 * 1.5 + 1/2 * 0.5 = 1,
# so the upper bound 1 is exact.
# Expected: valid.  The post used to become a function of r of its own, which the checker
# requires to be non-negative at every real r, so the bound was lost (unknown) although the
# preexpectation is the constant 1.
real r;
{
	r := 1.5;
}[1/2]{
	r := 0.5;
}
?Ex [r] <= 1
